## Features Implemented

| # | Feature | Status |
|---|---------|--------|
| 01 | Auth + Onboarding | ✅ Mock login triggers `fetchTransactions` + `fetchCryptoPrices` + `fetchRates` |
| 02 | Transaction Feed | ✅ 50 seeded transactions, category filter pills, emoji icons |
| 03 | Crypto Portfolio | ✅ Live CoinGecko prices for BTC/ETH/SOL, P/L calculations |
| 04 | Multi-currency Converter | ✅ **NEW** — live FX rates, 9 currencies, affects whole dashboard |
| 05 | Net Worth Dashboard | ✅ 60-second polling, zero business logic in component |
| 06 | Spending Insights | ✅ Budget utilization bar, `listenerMiddleware` fires notifications when over budget |

---

## Redux Architecture (All "Hard Rules" Met)

| Requirement | Implementation |
|-------------|----------------|
| 5+ Slices | `authSlice`, `portfolioSlice`, `currencySlice`, `transactionsSlice`, `notificationsSlice` |
| No API calls in components | All thunks in slices: `login`, `fetchTransactions`, `fetchCryptoPrices`, `fetchRates` |
| No derived state in components | All calculations in `createSelector` (portfolio value, net worth, spending totals) |
| Cross-slice side effects | `transactionsSlice` reacts to `login.fulfilled` · `portfolioSlice` reacts to `fetchRates.fulfilled` · `notificationsSlice` reacts to `fetchCryptoPrices.fulfilled` |
| `listenerMiddleware` | Budget exceeded → dispatches [addNotification](file:///Users/amoghp/Downloads/files/wealthledger/lib/store/slices/notificationsSlice.ts#28-46) when `fetchTransactions.fulfilled` |
| localStorage persistence | [currencyPersistenceMiddleware](file:///Users/amoghp/Downloads/files/wealthledger/lib/store/middleware/currencyPersistence.ts#4-19) saves `selectedCurrency` on every change |
| TypeScript everywhere | Strictly typed, no `any` |
| Smart/Dumb separation | Smart components read Redux; Dumb components only receive typed props |

